                  <p class="model__meta">{model.meta}</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              {model.body.map((p) => (
                <p class="model__p">{p}</p>
              ))}
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== A note for marketers ===== -->
  <section class="note-sec">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="note reveal">
        <span class="note__quote" aria-hidden="true">&#8220;</span>
        <span class="eyebrow note__eyebrow">A note for marketers</span>
        <p class="note__lead">
          You don't need to know how a diffusion model works internally to brief a great
          campaign. Same way you don't need to know how a CMOS sensor works to commission a
          photo shoot. But knowing the vocabulary changes the conversation with your studio,
          your agency, your internal stakeholders.
        </p>
        <p class="note__p">
          You ask sharper questions. You catch the difference between a tool with real craft
          behind it and one with a slick demo. And you save money, because most AIGC waste
          happens at the brief, long before anyone clicks "generate."
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

